From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangepi6 kernel-7 port
Subject: [PATCH] sched topology do not spread across CPUs of different capacities

On 7.3.5 one to four of eight busy threads sit on the little cores
(capacity 279) while big cores idle, costing ~12% on llama.cpp against
6.18. The board's domains are CLS (per cluster) under one MC domain with
ASYM_CPUCAPACITY across all 12 CPUs, and CLS still carries
SD_PREFER_SIBLING. 6.18's sd_init() cleared SD_PREFER_SIBLING on the
child of an asymmetric-capacity domain; 7.x no longer does. Load
balancing at MC takes prefer_sibling from the busiest group's flags (the
child's), so it evens nr_running across the five clusters, little one
included. Restore the 6.18 rule.
---
 kernel/sched/topology.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/topology.c b/kernel/sched/topology.c
index 3dab02539..90d2598bb 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/topology.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/topology.c
@@ -1999,6 +1999,17 @@ sd_init(struct sched_domain_topology_level *tl,
 	/*
 	 * Convert topological properties into behaviour.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * Sky1: don't attempt to spread across CPUs of different capacities.
+	 * 6.18 cleared SD_PREFER_SIBLING on the child of an asymmetric-capacity
+	 * domain; 7.x dropped that. Load balancing at the asymmetric level
+	 * reads the busiest group's flags (the child's), so with the flag kept
+	 * it evens nr_running across the clusters and parks busy threads on
+	 * the little cores while big cores idle.
+	 */
+	if ((sd->flags & SD_ASYM_CPUCAPACITY) && sd->child)
+		sd->child->flags &= ~SD_PREFER_SIBLING;
+
 	if (sd->flags & SD_SHARE_CPUCAPACITY) {
 		sd->imbalance_pct = 110;
 
